{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> The meaning: it is possible that its sense is, \"the mountains may depart, but my kindness from you shall not depart, and my covenant of peace between me and you\" — the meaning being like a man and his wife, between whom is a covenant of peace:" "<b>תמוטינה.</b> Like תשובינה (Ezekiel 16:55), for feminine forms in second-conjugation [binyan] verbs [nif'al] come on two patterns."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:30.979387825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}